cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the exact Gate A evidence-index digest reviewed. For a distributed copy,
  also cite the unique highest valid append-only receipt that exact-binds that
  same index, its canonical report, and packet Git commit. Treat publisher
  readback as an assertion unless a distinct independent transport record binds
  the same bytes. Until that record exists, independent transport verification
  is not established.
title: "Reiyah: HARBOR Gate A Research Architecture"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wahnich
    given-names: Daniel
repository-code: "https://github.com/manfromnowhere143/reiyah"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-08-25
abstract: >-
  An operator-unaccepted static Gate A correction candidate for the HARBOR
  research architecture. Version 1.2.0 is intended to make policy distributions,
  trajectory weights, causal identification, readiness unknown propagation, recovery event
  derivation, transfer eligibility, conformal guarantees, out-of-distribution and
  selective dispositions, population partitions, worst-group eligibility,
  human belief reconciliation, joint silent-miss identifiability, and assumption
  evidence eligibility executable against deterministic synthetic counterexamples.
  It adds no runtime, empirical result, safety claim, standards claim, or operator
  acceptance.
keywords:
  - automated driving
  - human automation interaction
  - uncertainty
  - causal inference
  - benchmark governance
